id: pm-xlb6aw
title: Telemetry worker permanently retries JSONB-incompatible Unicode events
description: "During verified Postgres reconnect recovery, a retained event containing a JSONB-incompatible Unicode value repeatedly raised SQLSTATE 22P05 and kept worker health failing. Preserve rejected raw JSON durably, acknowledge only after retention succeeds, and verify valid subsequent events still ingest. Reuse telemetry ingestion lineage; do not publish private deployment source or event data."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-05T12:38:33.401Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T12:49:39.618Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T12:46:37.156Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T12:46:37.156Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-5oj5
resolution: Durably retain JSONB-incompatible events before acknowledging their broker delivery
expected_result: "Rejected input must not retry forever or block following valid events, and original JSON must remain retained without duplicate aggregates"
actual_result: Real Unicode rejection replay retained one original JSON record for two identical inputs while all 23 valid events and aggregate finishes remained exact. Production worker is healthy with the rejected event retained
