comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-05T12:38:33.401Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status corpus plus request search and live open/in-progress lists found no Unicode rejection owner. pm-vhdc is closed UUID boundary validation; pm-rj3w is the active Postgres reconnect owner that exposed this independent poison-event path."
  "2026-09-05T12:45:20.317Z","harness:codex","Private acceptance passed: 21 expected rows recover after the disposable Postgres restart with unchanged worker PID; replay leaves 23 valid unique events and 23 aggregate finishes. Two identical JSONB-incompatible events produce exactly one retained original JSON row with SQLSTATE 22P05, and a subsequent valid barrier event ingests. Readiness and the real stale watchdog exit also pass. Private worker digest fc68db96312f9529ee42d4f6acedba5c74272353756e2328c8d0ba475ee098b7. Public CI does not execute this private operational drill; its evidence is separate from the product coverage claim."
  "2026-09-05T12:46:36.576Z","harness:codex","Deployment verified on the private telemetry host using a worker-only rebuild with saved rollback baselines. The readiness check is healthy; broker and recent database receipts confirm recovery. The original poison event is retained separately rather than counted as a successfully ingested command. Source, drill, health override and runbook remain intentionally ignored; reviewed public tracker records contain aggregate evidence only."
  "2026-09-05T12:49:39.618Z","harness:codex","PR 1199 review-round closeout: full quality:static, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 8444 tests, packed npm/Bun manual acceptance, package-artifact and docs-link gates pass. The latest pm-changelog package regenerated and verified CHANGELOG.md after structured closure. All active owners are released; the broader duplicate latency target remains open. Public source and private operational verification are recorded separately."
